# Docs — etude-9uf.3

The documentation work IS most of this bead. Deleting three scripts is nine
lines of `git rm`; the sweep is what makes the deletion honest, and ten of the
edit sites are prose.

## Docs changed, and why each one mattered

**`docs/plans/dogfood/review-gate-runbook.md`** — the important one. A live
judgement runbook whose §"Gate-JSON `reviewed_stages` must name an EXISTING run
stage" was stale on three counts:

1. it named `dogfood-close`, deleted here;
2. it asserted "A captured run has stages `plan/implement/verify/review` (NOT
   `docs` — docs is not a captured stage)";
3. it told the reader to map the docs-phase and final-review gates onto the
   `implement` diff stage.

Claims 2 and 3 were reversed by bead `etude-1od` two beads ago — `etude capture
docs --output docs-diff=<file>` creates a real docs stage, `etude gate` resolves
the reviewed stage by produced ROLE, and removing precisely that transport-only
alias was `etude-1od`'s stated purpose. So a live runbook was instructing readers
to do the thing this epic had just eliminated. Rewritten to the `etude capture` /
`etude gate` flow, preserving the constraint that still holds (capture the phase
before you gate it) and pointing at the supervisor runbook's stage/role table.

**`docs/plans/product/gate-reviewer-record-schema.md`** — two historical
citations. Reworded so the evidence stays checkable rather than deleted: they now
name the mechanism, the file, and the bead that removed it, so a reader can go to
the commit before `etude-9uf.3` and find the cited line. One was also in present
tense about a path that no longer exists; moved to past tense.

**`docs/plans/dogfood/retro-capture.md`** — "Manual dogfood capture supports
these retro triggers now" named the retired protocol as the live support for
triggers that are still live. Repointed at the supervised model.

**`examples/summarize/README.md` (×2), `examples/summarize/walkthrough.sh`** —
the contrast between the generic example and the tracker-coupled capture still
has a point, so the retired mechanism is named rather than the file path.

**`.beads/hooks/pre-push`** — the operator-facing BLOCKED message. Not
documentation in the `docs/` sense, but it is the only instruction most people
will ever read from this bead's subject area, and it pointed at a script that no
longer exists. It now points at `etude capture` / `etude gate` and the supervisor
runbook. Two test assertions pin it: that the new pointer is present, and that
the old script name is absent.

**`Makefile`** — the `pre-push-test` comment. It initially inherited the same
"that hook is live" claim the verify artifact had to retract, and now states what
the suite actually drives, with a pointer to bead `etude-6d9`.

**`scripts/dogfood-gate-capture.sh`, `scripts/dogfood-completeness-audit.sh`,
`internal/bench/corpus_runrefs.go`** — comments in surviving files that named or
present-tensed the deleted mechanism.

## What is deliberately NOT changed

Ten enumerated no-op sites, listed in the verify artifact: the bead id
`etude-dogfood-capture-protocol` (a permanent tracker handle, 5 sites),
historical retro-ledger entries, and protocol-name mentions in design notes.
Rewriting a ledger to match the present is the opposite of what a ledger is for.

## No new documentation was written

This bead removes a mechanism; the model that replaces it was documented by bead
`.2` in `docs/plans/dogfood/supervisor-runbook.md`, and the retro material that
survived the old protocol doc was extracted to `retro-capture.md` in the same
bead. There is nothing left to describe here — which is the point. The reason
`.2` came first was so that `.3` would have somewhere to point.

## Checks

`make docs-check` and `make docs-reality` green. The `docs-reality` check
compares documented commands against the shipped CLI; the rewritten runbook
section names `etude capture` and `etude gate`, both of which exist.

